.TH COOP 1 "" "coop" "coop Manual"
.SH NAME
coop \- run coding agents in an isolated box for your project.
.SH DESCRIPTION
The complete command reference. \fBcoop help \-\-all\fR prints the same text, followed by a page for each preset you can run in the current project.
.PP
.nf
coop: run coding agents in an isolated box for your project.

Usage: coop <command> [<args>...]

THE BOX: an isolated environment for running commands in this project
  coop run -- <command>             run a command in the box
  coop shell                        open a shell in the box

RUN AGENTS: work with a coding agent or a team of agents
  coop <claude|codex|gemini|grok>   start Claude, Codex, Gemini, or Grok
  coop <preset>                     run agents together using a preset
  coop <target> --peer <target>...  start with read-only peer agents

  A target is an agent, optionally with a model, effort and account:
  codex:gpt-6-astra/xhigh@work

ACCOUNTS, MODELS & PRESETS: choose the accounts and models your agents use
  coop login <agent>                sign in to an agent
  coop credentials [<agent>]        show your signed-in accounts
  coop models [<agent>]             show available models
  coop usage [<agent>]              show limits and a 30-day API estimate
  coop presets [<name>]             show your presets

TASKS: each task is a folder in .agent/tasks/
  coop tasks ls                     show tasks grouped by status
  coop tasks watch                  follow task progress
  coop tasks add "<title>"          add a task
  coop tasks decisions              show tasks waiting for your decision
  coop backlog                      save ideas for later
  coop context [<path>...]          show instructions and docs for your files

LOOPS: work through tasks automatically; configure the steps in .agent/loop.yaml
  coop loop [<target|preset>]       run agents until the queue is done

EVALUATIONS: check whether a model, preset or loop change helped
  coop eval                         run repeatable checks and compare results

FORKS: work in separate project copies, then review and merge the changes
  coop fork <name> <target|preset>  start an agent in a new fork
  coop fork ls                      show this project's forks
  coop fork review <name>           review a fork's changes
  coop fork merge <name>            merge a fork's changes into this branch
  coop fork merge --all             merge all forks into this branch
  coop fork logs [<name>]           show loop logs for one or all forks
  coop fork rm <name>               delete a fork
  coop fork stop <name>             stop a fork's background loop
  coop fork open <name>             open a fork in your editor
  coop fork path <name>             print a fork's directory path

SERVICES: databases and other services defined in .agent/compose.yml
  coop init --services              choose services to add
  coop up                           start services
  coop down                         stop services

SECURITY & ISOLATION: control access, check isolation, and protect secrets
  coop doctor                       check that the box's isolation works
  coop approve                      review and approve requested project access
  coop net                          manage this project's network access
  coop check-secrets                check project files for exposed secrets
  coop sign                         sign unpushed commits with your host key

SETUP & MAINTENANCE: set up projects and manage Coop on this machine
  coop init                         set up Coop in this project
  coop build                        rebuild the box
  coop update                       update Coop and the box
  coop version                      show the installed Coop version

INTEGRATIONS: use Coop with other tools and your shell
  coop help acp                     connect Coop to your editor
  coop help sessions                let other apps start and manage agents
  coop help prompt                  add Coop status to your shell prompt or tmux
  coop help completion              enable tab completion in Bash or Zsh

Help and examples: coop help <command>
Full reference:    coop help --all
Documentation:     https://coop.dryga.com/docs.html

==============================================================================

coop run: run a command in the box

Usage:
  coop run [<options>] -- <command> [<args>...]

OPTIONS
  --egress <mode>        network access: filtered (default), open or offline
  --allow-domain <host>  allow TLS to this exact host on port 443; repeatable
  --egress-rules <path>  add the network rules in this file

  Put Coop options before --. Everything after it belongs to your command.
  Without --, Coop options end where your command starts.

EXAMPLES
  coop run -- npm test
  coop run --egress open -- curl https://example.com
  coop run --egress offline -- git status

NETWORK ACCESS
  filtered  allow only what approved network rules permit (default)
  open      allow unrestricted internet access
  offline   block internet access

  Without --egress, the box is filtered unless the project's network
  setting or COOP_EGRESS chooses another mode. With --egress open or
  offline, the project's network rules do not apply to that run.

RULES FILE
  The file uses an egress_rules key, like box.egress_rules in
  .agent/project.yaml:

    egress_rules:
      - to: {domain: "docs.example.com"}
        protocol: tls
        ports: [443]

  Keep the file outside the project, where the agent cannot edit it.
  A file inside the project only requests access.

For more details see:
  coop help net

==============================================================================

coop shell: open a shell in the box

Usage:
  coop shell [<options>]

OPTIONS
  --egress <mode>        network access: filtered (default), open or offline
  --allow-domain <host>  allow TLS to this exact host on port 443; repeatable
  --egress-rules <path>  add the network rules in this file

EXAMPLES
  coop shell
  coop shell --egress open
  coop shell --egress offline

USING THE SHELL
  The shell opens in your project inside the box.
  Type exit or press Ctrl-D to return to your host.

NETWORK ACCESS
  filtered  allow only what approved network rules permit (default)
  open      allow unrestricted internet access
  offline   block internet access

  Without --egress, the box is filtered unless the project's network
  setting or COOP_EGRESS chooses another mode. With --egress open or
  offline, the project's network rules do not apply to that run.

For more details see:
  coop help net

