coop claude: run Claude in the box

Usage:
  coop claude[:<model>][/<effort>][@<account>] [<options>] [-- <claude-args>...]

OPTIONS
  --peer <target>        start a read-only peer agent (no @account); repeatable
  -p "<prompt>"          run one prompt and exit
  --                     pass all remaining arguments directly to Claude

NETWORK OPTIONS
  --egress <mode>        network access: filtered (default), open or offline
  --allow-domain <host>  allow TLS to this exact host on port 443; repeatable
  --egress-rules <path>  add the network rules in this file

EXAMPLES
  coop claude
  coop claude:opus
  coop claude:opus/high@work
  coop claude -p "fix the failing test"
  coop claude -- --help

MODELS AND ACCOUNTS
  coop models claude       list Claude models
  coop credentials claude  list Claude accounts
  coop login claude        sign in to Claude

For a guide to using multiple models and providers together:
  coop help presets

