coop fork: let an agent work in a separate copy of your project

Usage: coop fork <name> [<target|preset>] [<options>]
       coop fork <command> [<args>...]

START WORK
  coop fork myfork claude        create a fork and start Claude
  coop fork myfork               continue an existing fork's session
  coop fork myfork frontier      use a preset
  coop fork myfork claude -d     work through tasks in the background

REVIEW AND MERGE
  ls             show forks and their progress
  review <name>  review a fork's changes
  merge <name>   merge its commits into your current branch
  merge --all    merge eligible forks one at a time

MANAGE
  logs [<name>]  show one fork's logs, or all forks
  stop <name>    stop a fork's background loop
  open <name>    open a fork in your editor
  path <name>    print its folder path
  rm <name>      delete a fork

SESSION OPTIONS
  --isolated      create independent Git storage and require reviewed
                  publication
  -c, --continue  continue the last session (default when reopening)
  --new           start a new conversation in the existing fork
  --fresh         delete the fork and its service data, then recreate it
  -f, --force     with --fresh, stop active work and discard unmerged changes
  -y, --yes       with --fresh, skip confirmation

  An isolated fork stays that way when reopened, looped or used over ACP.
  Existing forks are not converted, and isolation is off by default.
  Review it with coop fork review; --force cannot bypass its policy.

NETWORK OPTIONS
  --egress <mode>        network access: filtered (default), open or offline
  --allow-domain <host>  allow TLS to this exact host on port 443; repeatable
  --egress-rules <path>  add the network rules in this file

LOOP OPTIONS
  --loop                 work through the project's task queue
  -d, --detach           run the loop in the background (implies --loop)
  -t, --tasks <path>     choose a task queue; repeat for more queues
  --peer <target>        start a read-only peer agent (no @account); repeatable

  Each fork receives one project task at a time. Its task is completed in the
  project queue when you merge the reviewed work. Stopping keeps it resumable.

EDITOR INTEGRATION
  coop fork <name> acp  use an existing fork from an ACP editor

Model and account syntax: coop help models
Command options:          coop help fork <command>

